before:
The one-column map stacks the same elements in their existing source order. A media query can choose between these maps based on available viewport width.
```css
.demo { writing-mode: horizontal-tb; direction: ltr; }
.layout { display: grid; width: 240px; grid-template-columns: 240px; grid-template-areas: "title" "nav" "content"; } header { grid-area: title; } nav { grid-area: nav; } main { grid-area: content; }
```

after:
The supplied page has a title, navigation, and main content. This map puts the title above the other two parts.
```css
.layout {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 80px 160px;
  grid-template-areas:
    "title title"
    "nav content";
}
header { grid-area: title; }
nav { grid-area: nav; }
main { grid-area: content; }
```
